1. Purpose

Test time-interpolated prolongation of a non-evolved, two-time-level grid
function across mesh-refinement (coarse/fine) boundaries while the fine level
is mid-subcycle and thus misaligned in time with its parent coarse level.

The field w(t,x,y,z) = (a + b x + c y + d z) t is linear in both time and
space, so with "linear extrapolation" outer boundaries the only ghost cells
that can be wrong are the coarse/fine boundary ghosts. Without temporal
interpolation in the prolongation those ghosts carry an O(dt) error at the
misaligned (odd) output iterations; with the fix the error is round-off.
